# lf114, the name-keeping country printer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf114
revision 2
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent none
tier full
written_for tn_sm_dun_harvestley
written_by claude-codex-lf-1
title the name-keeping country printer
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=merchant
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk remembers_every_name_ever_heard
likes warm_bread digging new_boots thunder
dislikes rats gulls
fears a_press_fire_started_by_careless_embers a_name_printed_wrong_on_an_order
hopes every_wage_is_paid_on_time a_clean_press_for_the_next_generation
topics work +0.5 memories +0.4 prices +0.3 travel +0.2
styles comfort=attentive gossip=discreet refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# runs the #press#, remembers each #name# that crosses the #counter#, and knows the #road# to the city by walking it.

words
oath! = By type and tally | Ink on my paws
saying! = A name is worth setting straight | Read the proof before the run
press = press | country press
paper = paper | mill paper
sheet = sheet | clean sheet
sheets = sheets | stacked sheets
page = page | printed page
pages = pages | finished pages
type = type | metal type
letter = letter | small letter
letters = letters | set letters
line = line | printed line
lines = lines | even lines
proof = proof | first proof
form = form | locked form
frame = frame | press frame
plate = plate | inked plate
ink = ink | black ink
roller = roller | ink roller
tray = tray | type tray
case = case | letter case
block = block | type block
blocks = blocks | type blocks
pressman = pressman | working printer
hand = hand | press hand
hands = hands | press hands
work = work | printing work
order = order | print order
orders = orders | town orders
book = book | order book
books = books | bound books
ledger = ledger | wage ledger
wage = wage | weekly wage
wages = wages | earned wages
name = name | remembered name
names = names | remembered names
visitor = visitor | new visitor
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
traveller = traveller | road traveller
stranger = stranger | passing stranger
friend = friend | old friend
buyer = buyer | waiting buyer
customer = customer | local customer
counter = counter | shop counter
shelf = shelf | front shelf
shop = shop | small shop
stairs = stairs | steep stairs
flat = flat | upstairs flat
roof = roof | sound roof
door = door | front door
window = window | upper window
road = road | long road
mile = mile | road mile
miles = miles | many miles
city = city | far city
market = market | city market
wagon = wagon | supply wagon
cart = cart | goods cart
load = load | paper load
price = price | posted price
cost = cost | wagon cost
coin = coin | counted coin
light = light | lamp light
lamp = lamp | counter lamp
fire = fire | press fire
ash = ash | cold ash
rat = rat | store rat
rats = rats | hungry rats
gull = gull | crying gull
gulls = gulls | roof gulls
bread = bread | warm bread
oven = oven | baker oven
larder = larder | small larder
boot = boot | new boot
boots = boots | new boots
garden = garden | back garden
spade = spade | garden spade
soil = soil | dark soil
thunder = thunder | distant thunder
storm = storm | coming storm
rain = rain | heavy rain
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | late evening
night = night | quiet night
day = day | long day
hour = hour | working hour
hours = hours | long hours
queue = queue | waiting queue
festival = festival | town festival
watch = watch | town watch
gate = gate | town gate
roadwork = roadwork | road repairs
wagons = wagons | late wagons
seat = seat | front seat
sample = sample | printed sample
samples = samples | printed samples
prices = prices | posted prices
print = print | fresh print
stack = stack | paper stack
proofs = proofs | first proofs
lesson = lesson | press lesson

any
opinion @1 city against 1 : I reached the #city# on foot and found a crowd that knew no #names#. | It swallowed a whole #day# of mine.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A paid #hand# may still need #bread# in a thin week. | Keep a #larder# open for them.
opinion @1 merchants for 1 : I keep a #counter# myself; every #wagon# adds to the #cost#. | I still show the #price# before a sale.
opinion @1 newcomers for 2 : A new #hand# who learns the #case# can stay. | A #name# belongs in the #book# when the work is good.
opinion @1 road against 1 : Late #wagons# leave the #press# still when it should be running. | I would put #coin# toward the #roadwork#.
opinion @1 strangers for 2 : A #traveller# can bring a fresh #order# and a story. | I ask their #name# before the ink dries.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : The #watch# keeps wandering paws away from my #counter#. | I lock the #door# too.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : The #festival# fills my #order# #book#. | I enjoy its quiet end more than its noise.
opinion @1 times mixed 0 : The #press# runs when it has #paper# and #hands#. | I cannot promise the #road# will cooperate.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I believe I know your #name#. | #greet#. Give me a moment to set down this #proof#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : The #bread# is still warm upstairs. | You may take the #seat# by my #counter#.
line @1 greet.return : I kept your last #order# under the #book#. | Your #name# came to me before your face.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #lamp# is still burning over the first #proof#. | #greet#. The #press# wakes early today.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Come upstairs when the #press# stops. | There is #bread# left by the #window#.
line @1 again.open : I had found the missing #letter#. | Were we speaking of the #road#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must check the next #proof#. | Take care on those #stairs#.
line @1 farewell.return : The #pages# may be ready when you return. | Next time I will remember your #order# as well.
line @1 react.news : Start with the #name#, if you know it. | I can stop sorting #type# and listen.
line @1 react.news.new : That has not reached the #shop# yet. | Who carried this along the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard a shorter account from the #wagon#. | You have added the missing #line#.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would want to see the written #order#. | Who put a #name# to that claim?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I am sorry. Sit beside the #lamp# a moment. | I will close the #book# and hear you.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That #name# deserves a fresh #page#. | I have #bread# upstairs for this news.
line @1 answer.how : The #press# is sound; I found a #rat# near the #paper#. | Better since the #wagon# arrived.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I am locking this #form# before it shifts. | Let me finish one #page#.
line @1 ask.how : Did you find a dry #road# in? | Has your #work# brought you a new #name#?
line @1 sympathise : I can hear you after this #sheet#. | Have some warm #bread# and stay under the #roof#.
line @1 reassure : I will put your #name# beside the next #order#. | We can put the #page# right before it goes out.
line @1 decline : I will not print a #name# without checking it. | The #press# cannot run with that #plate# loose.
line @1 accept_decline : I understand; I can hold the #paper# here. | Then I will close the #book# for today.
line @1 thank : You spotted the reversed #letter# in time. | That new #boot# saved me a cold walk.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I happened to have the #case# open already. | A proper #proof# is part of my #work#.
line @1 preclose : The #ink# must be covered overnight. | I still owe the #hands# their #wages#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : I remember your #name# better than you remember your #orders#. | Mind my #stairs#; they enjoy surprises.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. The #lines# are straight now. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will recheck the #book#.
line @1 give.advice : Read a #proof# in daylight before paying for a full run. | Keep your #paper# dry beneath the #roof#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep your #coin# close on the #road#. | Let the #wagon# travel with company.
scene clean_proof
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I read the #proof# against the #window# before the full run. | A reversed #letter# is easier to fix while the #press# is still.
b : Do you always find mistakes? | Who checks it?
a : Enough to keep looking. | Another #hand# reads it too.

scene set_type
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I place each #letter# from the #case# into its #line#. | A loose #block# can spoil a whole #page#.
b : Do your hands ache? | Does it take long?
a : After a long run. | Longer than most expect.

scene ink_roller
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Too much #ink# on the #roller# fills the small #letters#. | I roll it thin across the #plate#.
b : Can you wipe it away? | Who taught you?
a : Before the #sheet# dries. | An older #pressman#.

scene paper_from_vat
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The vat #hands# send #paper# with different edges. | I choose the even #sheets# for a close #line# of #type#.
b : What becomes of the rest? | Do they mind?
a : Broader #pages#. | They know why I ask.

scene locked_form
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I tap the #form# gently before the first pull. | A shifting #letter# leaves a mark across every copy.
b : Does it often move? | Can you tell at once?
a : Only if rushed. | On the first #proof#.

scene drying_pages
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fresh #pages# need space where air can pass. | I keep them clear of the #lamp# and its flame.
b : How many fit? | What if it rains?
a : One run at a time. | Under the sound #roof#.

scene bound_book
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A finished #book# hides a great many small decisions. | I still notice which #page# took three tries.
b : Do readers notice? | Is that satisfying?
a : Usually not. | Once it closes well.

scene wrong_name
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have remembered a #name# after one visit and misheard its spelling. | I ask for it twice before it reaches the #press#.
b : Did anyone mind? | Do you remember mine?
a : One buyer did. | Yes, I believe I do.

scene old_customer
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #customer# returned after years with a changed #order#. | The #name# came back to me before the old #page# did.
b : Did you tell them? | Did they recognize you?
a : Only after checking. | They remembered the #shop#.

scene new_hand
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Speed is the last thing I ask of a #hand# at the #case#. | I ask for careful #lines# first.
b : How do you teach? | Do mistakes cost much?
a : One #tray# at a time. | Only if they leave the #press#.

scene wage_book
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep the #wage# #book# beside the #orders#. | A worker should see the count behind each payment.
b : Do they ask? | Is the count simple?
a : They may whenever they wish. | It rarely feels so.

scene posted_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I write the #price# beside each #sample# #page#. | A buyer should know the #cost# before the #press# begins.
b : Does it change? | What adds to it?
a : When #paper# is scarce. | A late #wagon#.

scene late_wagon
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #wagon# from the #city# arrived after the #light# was gone. | I kept the #press# closed until I checked the #load#.
b : Was it damaged? | Did you wait outside?
a : A few #sheets# were wet. | Under the #gate# lamp.

scene walk_to_city
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I once walked to the #city# and returned by the same #road#. | The noise there followed me halfway home.
b : Why walk? | Would you go again?
a : The #cart# was full. | Only with an #order#.

scene road_miles
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #mile# feels longer when a promised #load# does not come. | I know each turn from waiting for #wagons#.
b : Do you travel often? | What is the worst stretch?
a : Less than I used to. | The low ground after #rain#.

scene watch_round
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #watch# passes my #door# before I cover the #ink#. | I can hear their steps from upstairs.
b : Does that comfort you? | Do you lock up?
a : It does. | Every #night#.

scene rat_in_store
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #rat# got behind the bottom #shelf# and chewed the #paper#. | I found the damage by the torn corner.
b : Did you catch it? | Was much lost?
a : Not yet. | Only the outside #sheets#.

scene gulls_on_roof
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #gulls# wake before the #press# does. | One likes to shout above my #window#.
b : Can you drive it off? | Do you mind the sound?
a : Not for long. | More than the #thunder#.

scene warm_bread
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I bring #bread# upstairs while it is still warm. | It makes the #flat# feel less like a second #shop#.
b : Do you bake it? | Do you share?
a : The baker has that skill. | Whenever someone is here.

scene garden_spade
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Digging with a #spade# asks a different rhythm than setting #type#. | I go to the #garden# when a #proof# will not settle in my head.
b : Does it help? | What grows there?
a : Often. | What the #soil# permits.

scene new_boots
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A new pair of #boots# makes an old #road# feel shorter. | I save them for the wet stretch beyond the #gate#.
b : Do they last? | Why keep the old pair?
a : If I care for them. | For the #garden#.

scene thunder_roof
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #thunder# when the #roof# is sound. | The #press# rests while I listen from upstairs.
b : Does it frighten you? | What about the paper?
a : I like hearing it from here. | I keep it dry.

scene festival_order
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Before the #festival# every #shop# asks for another printed #page#. | Afterward I enjoy the empty #queue#.
b : Do you celebrate? | Is it good for business?
a : At its quieter edge. | It keeps the #hands# paid.

scene visitor_names
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I write a #visitor# in memory before I enter an #order# in the #book#. | The face sometimes takes longer to return.
b : Do you ever forget? | Is that useful?
a : I have to ask again sometimes. | Especially at the #counter#.

scene printer_fire
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I keep hot #ash# far from the dry #sheets#. | A small #fire# could take the whole #press#.
b : Has one started? | Who checks at night?
a : Never here. | I make the last round.

scene stair_count
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #stairs# to my #flat# sound different under a loaded #hand#. | I know when the #paper# delivery has arrived.
b : Can you tell whose steps? | Does it wake you?
a : Sometimes. | Only the #gulls# do that.

scene quiet_counter
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like the #counter# after the final #customer# leaves. | Then I can hear whether the #press# has begun to rattle.
b : Does it rattle often? | Do you rest then?
a : Only a loose #block#. | After I check it.

story first_proof [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : My first paid #proof# had one reversed #letter# in the heading.
  : A buyer spotted it before I did.
  b : That is a useful lesson. Did you repair it?
  : I reset the #line# before the #press# ran.

story road_walk [topic=travel self.age>=18]
  : I walked the full #road# to the #city# because the #wagon# was full.
  : Coming home I could still hear the city #market# behind me.
  b : A long way on foot. Did you return with anything?
  : A little #paper# and a great wish for quiet.

story remembered_name [topic=memories self.age>=18]
  : A #traveller# came back years after a single #order#.
  : I recalled the #name# and forgot what I had printed.
  ask : Did that please them?
  b : Memory works strangely.
  : It did once I found the old #book#.

story night_rat [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : After closing, a #rat# scratched behind the #shelf#.
  : It had torn a corner from the first #sheet# in a fresh #stack#.
  ask : Did it get away?
  b : That is poor company.
  : It did, but I moved every #sheet# upstairs.

story thunder_proof [topic=weather self.age>=18]
  : A #storm# stopped the #wagon# while I held a finished #proof#.
  : I listened to #thunder# under a good #roof# and waited.
  ask : Did the buyer come?
  b : A fine place to wait.
  : The next #morning#, with dry #boots#.

rule @bark_proof
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Read the #proof# once more. | This #letter# faces the wrong way.

rule @bark_counter
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Your #order# is under the #book#. | Give me the #name# you want printed.

rule @bark_wagon
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say The #wagon# is late again. | Keep that #paper# beneath the cover.

rule @bark_rat
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 11h
say There is a #rat# behind the #shelf#. | Lift the bottom #stack# clear.

rule @bark_bread
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 12h
say The #bread# is warm upstairs. | I have set aside another #plate#.

rule @bark_thunder
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 13h
say That #thunder# sounds close. | The #roof# is holding well.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have your #name# in mind. | #greet#. The #press# is between runs.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I remember your last #order#. | You have returned before the #ink# is dry.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : You found me above the #press#; speak from the #door#. | Is this needed before #morning#?
dlg @1 resident.job : I run the #press# at #self.workplace#. | I set #type#, read #proofs#, and count the #orders#.
dlg @2 resident.job [self.working=yes] : I am setting a narrow #line# of #type#. | This #proof# needs another look.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I will cover the #ink#. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind the #stairs#.
dlg @1 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : #greet#. The #samples# and #prices# are here. | Tell me what you want on the #page#.
dlg @2 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : The #shelf# is bare, but I can take a future #order#. | The #wagon# has not brought fresh #paper#.
dlg @3 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The #press# is still for the #night#. | Come when the #counter# opens.
dlg @4 shop.greet [here.shop!=bare here.shop!=asleep] : #greet#. Ask to see a #sample# of the #print#. | I can price the #pages# at this #counter#.
dlg @1 shop.prices [here.shop=open|bare] : The #price# depends on #paper# and the number of #pages#. | I put each #cost# in the #book# before work begins.
dlg @1 shop.bye : #farewell#. Keep the #pages# under cover. | #shop_bye# I will mark your #order# here.
dlg @1 master.learn [here.teaches=yes] : Start with a single #letter# in the #case#. | I will show you how to read a #proof#.
dlg @2 master.learn [here.teaches=yes topic.meeting=known] : You returned for the next #lesson#. | The #line# you set yesterday held straight.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you remember names? -> names
node names
say I listen closely when a person gives me a #name# for an #order#.
free
choice Did you walk to the city? -> walk
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node walk
say Once, for a full #day#. The #road# felt quiet on the way home.
choice Back to the counter. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice Can you print an order? -> order
node order
say Show me the words and I will quote the #price# before setting #type#.
free
choice May I see the paper? -> paper
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node paper
say These #sheets# came from the vat nearby. Feel the edge before deciding.
choice Back to the shop. -> greet
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have cleared the #counter#. | #greet#. The first #proof# is ready.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must pay the #hands#. | The #pages# can dry while we rest.
